---
description: |
  Normalizes an Agentmetry event to OCSF.

  ```tql
  from_file "agentmetry-trail.jsonl" {
    read_ndjson
  }
  agentmetry::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  Agentmetry writes one JSON object per event, which Tenzir reads natively, so
  the package starts at the mapper. The operator accepts both forms the
  recorder emits: the canonical event that its webhook sink posts, and a line
  of its hash-chained trail, which wraps the same event. It maps each event to
  the OCSF class that fits it. Whatever has no OCSF attribute remains under
  `unmapped`.

  Callers who already hold a structured Agentmetry event under another field,
  or who want to inspect and enrich the event before mapping, use
  `agentmetry::ocsf::map`.
args:
  positional:
    - name: agentmetry
      description: The structured Agentmetry event.
      type: field
      default: this
  named:
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

$into.agentmetry = $agentmetry
agentmetry::ocsf::map $into.agentmetry, $into.ocsf
$into = $into.ocsf
